---
import "../styles/global.css";
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <title>ALPS Foundation — manifesto (draft)</title>
  </head>
  <body class="guide-page">
    <main class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-6 py-20 md:py-28">
      <p class="mb-10 rounded-sm border border-rule bg-paper-alt p-4 text-sm text-ink-soft">
        <span class="mb-1 block text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ink-soft/80">
          Draft — not linked from the site, for review only
        </span>
        Mission, vision, and activities, split out of the ethics charter so each document has one job.
        This one is <strong class="text-ink">who we are and what we do</strong>; the charter is
        <strong class="text-ink">how we behave</strong>.
      </p>

      <p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ink-soft">ALPS Foundation</p>
      <h1 class="mb-4 text-4xl font-black leading-tight tracking-tight md:text-5xl">Manifesto</h1>
      <p class="mb-10 text-lg text-ink">Who we are, what we believe, and what we do.</p>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="mb-4 border-b border-rule pb-2 text-xl font-semibold">Mission</h2>
        <p class="text-ink-soft">
          We educate professionals and society on psychedelic research and therapy, grounded in
          scientific literature and evidence-based practices. ALPS builds a collaborative platform for
          the psychedelic community, paving the way for sustainable psychedelic research, and safe,
          legal, and accessible therapeutic experiences. Our intrinsic motivation is to reduce suffering
          and promote positive human development.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="mb-4 border-b border-rule pb-2 text-xl font-semibold">Vision</h2>
        <p class="text-ink-soft">
          ALPS envisions a future where psychedelic research and therapy are integrated into mainstream
          mental health care, supported by sustainable organisations, rigorous research, and broad
          public engagement. We aim to promote safety, reduce stigma, and contribute to policy
          discussions on the responsible use of psychedelics.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="mb-4 border-b border-rule pb-2 text-xl font-semibold">Philosophy &amp; values</h2>
        <ul class="divide-y divide-rule text-ink-soft">
          <li class="py-3">
            <strong class="text-ink">Openness &amp; loving-kindness</strong> — we foster a culture of
            inclusion, trust, and compassion, encouraging all members to bring their authentic selves to
            their work and to our community.
          </li>
          <li class="py-3">
            <strong class="text-ink">Honesty &amp; responsibility</strong> — we value transparency,
            integrity, and shared responsibility, empowering teams through self-management and
            collaborative decision-making.
          </li>
          <li class="py-3">
            <strong class="text-ink">Rationality &amp; critical thinking</strong> — our actions are
            guided by scientific evidence, ongoing learning, and self-reflection, adapting as new
            opportunities and challenges arise.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="mb-4 border-b border-rule pb-2 text-xl font-semibold">Main activities</h2>
        <ul class="divide-y divide-rule text-ink-soft">
          <li class="py-3">
            <strong class="text-ink">Education</strong> — annual academic events (the Conference, Forum,
            and Summer School) open to practitioners, researchers, and the public.
          </li>
          <li class="py-3">
            <strong class="text-ink">Research</strong> — independent projects and university
            collaborations advancing psychedelic science.
          </li>
          <li class="py-3">
            <strong class="text-ink">Access</strong> — advising practitioners and facilitating access to
            psychedelic therapies within the Swiss legal framework.
          </li>
          <li class="py-3">
            <strong class="text-ink">Community &amp; media</strong> — building a national and global
            network, sharing knowledge through open-access media.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <div class="mb-12 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-4 rounded-sm border border-rule p-5">
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft">
          This is who we are and what we do. For the code of conduct that governs ALPS events and
          teaching, see our ethics charter.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/charter-draft"
          class="whitespace-nowrap border-b border-ink text-sm font-semibold text-ink hover:border-ink-soft hover:text-ink-soft"
        >
          Read the ethics charter →
        </a>
      </div>

      <footer class="border-t border-rule pt-8 text-xs text-ink-soft/80">
        <p>
          Draft prepared from the ALPS Task List item "Charter / One-Pager" and Drive sources
          "One-Pager Content" and ALPS_One_Pager_25-07-29.pdf.
        </p>
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
